<p><font class="dinertitle"><b>Forum Rules</b></font><br>25 April 2002</font></p><center><b>Forum Code of Conduct</b></center> <br /><br />Below is the basic set of guidelines used by the Moderators of the forums here, with our growth and nearly reaching 3000 registered users it is increasingly important to make sure everyone is aware of our polocies and hopefully stop problems before they start and make the Staff's job a little easier, and our users' trolling more enjoyable. <br /><br /><b>Minor Offenses</b>-No action taken. <br /><br />1. <i>Improper forum posting</i>-This is posting in a forum that your post is not ment for. We have created several different forums so that people who wish to discuss the topic can do so and people who dont, dont have to. So please use the appropriate forums. If you by accident or design post in the wrong forum your post will be moved to a more appropriate one, but you will not be penalized in any way for this. <br /><br />2. <i>Cross-posting</i>-This is the creation of the same topic in more then one forum. When this happens the one in the most appropriate forum will remain and all others deleted. You will not be penalized in any way for Cross-posting. <br /><br />3.<i>Advertising</i>-Posts containing nothing but pure advertisement are subject to deletion without warning. Its fine to give someone a suggestion about something if they request, as part of a post, as advice, etc. But pure advertisment on the boards will not be allowed. You will not be penalized in any way however for advertising. <br /><br /><br /><b>Moderate Offenses</b>-Warning first time and possible further action if persists. <br /><br />1. <i>Spamming</i>-This is the creating of posts with absolutly no content or purpose other then to take up board space. It may also be consider spam to recreate a post that has "died" or to bump a post, depending on the situation. With the exception of the Market forum, where you can bump your post till the cows come home :p <br /><br />2. <i>Post-beefing</i>-This is creating multiple usernames and then using those names in the same thread or in threads of the same topic and pretending to be a different person in order to build false support for your views and opinions. Your IP is logged at every posting, so post-beefers are easily spotted. This is a place for REAL people to come and discuss, please leave the talking to yourself for the mirror  In the case of post-beefing the offender will be warned both via EMail and in the topic which he/she is beefing, and thus the multiple usernames will be reveiled as one to the public. <br /><br />3. <i>Inappropriate Content</i>-Inappropriate content is subjective, and therefor difficult to pin down in words. We try to be as open as possible in allowing expression, but there is a certain line that must be upheld to keep the place within acceptable standards. Inappripriate content is therefor a judgement call by the Mods. Something that may be considered inappropriate are: Overly sexual pictures, overly graphic pictures, and the like. If you have a questionable pic you want viewed, then do not post it directly, make a link. We do not consider ourselves responsible for out of site content, so you can link pretty much whatever you want in your post, as long as you post a warning if it is something that you think may be considered "Inappropriate", if you do not post a warning wether by choice or because you felt it was not warrented, a warning may be built in for you by Mods. Because of the subjectivity of inappropriate content, you probably wont get a warning the first time you post something "inappropriate". <br /><br />4. <i>Circumventing the Staff</i>-This is the undoing of something a Mod has done or redoing of something a Mod has requested you not to do. IE: They move your post and you repost it in the forum they moved it from. There really wouldn't be much point in even attempting to Moderate the forums if this kind of thing were tolerated. Mods are just trying to keep the forum so that all can enjoy it, please cooperate with them and respect that. <br /><br /><b>Major Offenses-Immediate Banning.</b> <br /><br />1. <i>Flood Attacks</i>-This is the flooding of forum(s) with spam in order to disrupt the boards. Such posts will be deleted on sight by Mods until an Admin can get online to issue a banning to the offending party. <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2"><tr>
